1
00:00:05,259 --> 00:00:08,259
[Aoi Toudou] The hands
will never surpass the eyes.

2
00:00:08,342 --> 00:00:11,009
Unless you cultivate the
eyes to discern good from bad,

3
00:00:11,092 --> 00:00:13,801
you cannot hope
to improve the hands

4
00:00:13,884 --> 00:00:15,050
that create works of art.

5
00:00:18,343 --> 00:00:21,802
It's a phrase that's often
used among creators,

6
00:00:21,885 --> 00:00:23,319
but it applies to
all kinds of fields.

7
00:00:23,343 --> 00:00:25,802
Those with good
eyes will improve

8
00:00:25,885 --> 00:00:27,286
far more rapidly
than those without!

9
00:00:27,344 --> 00:00:29,011
(energetic music)

10
00:00:29,094 --> 00:00:32,094
(grunting)

11
00:00:42,345 --> 00:00:45,136
When I throw my
right horizontal punch...

12
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,679
he immediately
sends a left vertical jab!

13
00:00:48,846 --> 00:00:51,346
Itadori wasn't moving
like this before!

14
00:00:51,429 --> 00:00:52,471
He's improving...

15
00:00:53,221 --> 00:00:55,304
by devouring me!

16
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,346
(grunting)

17
00:00:57,429 --> 00:01:00,472
What a beautiful way
to knock me down!

18
00:01:01,597 --> 00:01:03,138
[Yuuji Itadori] His
face is wide open!

19
00:01:03,222 --> 00:01:04,264
I can hit it!

20
00:01:05,806 --> 00:01:07,138
Even with Divergent Fist!

21
00:01:10,139 --> 00:01:11,306
(gasps)

22
00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:13,306
Somehow he stopped
my fist with his forehead

23
00:01:13,390 --> 00:01:15,098
before it could
reach full speed!

24
00:01:16,265 --> 00:01:19,974
That's not exactly what I
want you to devour right now.

25
00:01:20,056 --> 00:01:23,891
Your Divergent Fist is
created by your cursed energy

26
00:01:23,975 --> 00:01:26,224
lagging slightly behind your
superhuman physical prowess,

27
00:01:26,307 --> 00:01:29,182
when normally
there'd be no lag at all.

28
00:01:29,266 --> 00:01:31,557
It's a tricky move.

29
00:01:31,641 --> 00:01:33,602
Your average sorcerer
wouldn't know what happened,

30
00:01:33,642 --> 00:01:35,767
and they'd be left disoriented.

31
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:37,183
It has lots of force, too.

32
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:40,017
Enough for opponents
on that level, at least.

33
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:40,892
(gasps)

34
00:01:40,976 --> 00:01:44,268
But it won't work
against special-grades.

35
00:01:44,351 --> 00:01:46,059
What will you do, best friend?

36
00:01:48,476 --> 00:01:52,101
I'll use my full strength and
imbue it with cursed energy.

37
00:01:52,184 --> 00:01:53,727
Good!

38
00:01:53,811 --> 00:01:56,894
If that's so, why is your
cursed energy lagging?

39
00:01:56,978 --> 00:01:57,727
I know why!

40
00:01:57,811 --> 00:01:59,143
It's because you're
channeling it!

41
00:02:01,310 --> 00:02:03,727
Huh?

42
00:02:03,811 --> 00:02:07,311
Wait, I thought we were
talking about channeling it faster.

43
00:02:07,395 --> 00:02:09,061
When we channel cursed energy,

44
00:02:09,144 --> 00:02:10,979
it is a technique
that most sorcerers

45
00:02:11,061 --> 00:02:12,770
are conscious of doing.

46
00:02:12,853 --> 00:02:14,228
My stomach's full of rage,

47
00:02:14,311 --> 00:02:16,813
or, the blood is
boiling in my gut.

48
00:02:16,896 --> 00:02:18,396
The theory is that cursed energy

49
00:02:18,479 --> 00:02:21,145
extracted from such negative
emotions starts in the navel

50
00:02:21,229 --> 00:02:23,813
and is channeled
throughout the body.

51
00:02:23,896 --> 00:02:26,563
They say it flows from
the navel to the chest,

52
00:02:26,647 --> 00:02:29,855
then to the shoulders,
arms, and finally the fists.

53
00:02:31,146 --> 00:02:33,605
But this view of the
body as individual parts

54
00:02:33,689 --> 00:02:35,397
is what delays cursed energy.

55
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,773
The idea of channeling
cursed energy isn't wrong,

56
00:02:38,856 --> 00:02:40,356
but that's only the first step.

57
00:02:40,439 --> 00:02:43,773
You can't let yourself remain
too trapped by that concept.

58
00:02:43,856 --> 00:02:45,773
The better the
sorcerer, the harder it is

59
00:02:45,856 --> 00:02:47,856
to read the flow of
their cursed energy.

60
00:02:49,107 --> 00:02:51,983
Yours is hard to read
for a different reason.

61
00:02:52,065 --> 00:02:54,399
Would you say sorcerers
think using their guts?

62
00:02:55,565 --> 00:02:58,357
Do we express
anger with our heads?

63
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,108
Now listen to me, Itadori.

64
00:03:00,191 --> 00:03:01,108
(gasps)

65
00:03:01,191 --> 00:03:02,650
(eagle screeches)

66
00:03:02,733 --> 00:03:05,316
(moving orchestral music)

67
00:03:11,985 --> 00:03:14,484
We exist in this world
with our entire mind,

68
00:03:14,567 --> 00:03:16,859
body, and soul as one whole.

69
00:03:16,943 --> 00:03:19,484
It's such a given that no
one even thinks about it.

70
00:03:26,443 --> 00:03:27,694
Thank you, Toudou.

71
00:03:29,318 --> 00:03:30,318
I think now...

72
00:03:31,569 --> 00:03:32,569
I understand.

73
00:03:33,987 --> 00:03:34,987
Good.

74
00:03:35,028 --> 00:03:37,444
Then no more words are needed.

75
00:03:37,528 --> 00:03:38,945
I won't hold back!

76
00:03:44,404 --> 00:03:48,279
I'll guide you with
my full strength!

77
00:03:48,362 --> 00:03:49,362
Don't die on me, Itadori!

78
00:03:49,404 --> 00:03:52,529
Rise up to greater heights!

79
00:03:54,571 --> 00:03:59,863
(Opening theme music)

80
00:03:59,947 --> 00:04:03,488
(singing in Japanese)

81
00:05:23,538 --> 00:05:27,329
(birds whistling)

82
00:05:27,413 --> 00:05:29,204
Hey, you!

83
00:05:29,288 --> 00:05:32,747
Your old fart Principal told
you to kill Itadori, didn't he?

84
00:05:32,831 --> 00:05:33,998
(gasps)

85
00:05:34,080 --> 00:05:36,455
This girl has good intuition!

86
00:05:36,539 --> 00:05:38,580
No, Panda who figured that out.

87
00:05:39,622 --> 00:05:40,497
Huh? What are you saying?

88
00:05:40,580 --> 00:05:43,790
You don't need to try
and hide it from me.

89
00:05:43,873 --> 00:05:46,040
I'm out to kill someone, too.

90
00:05:46,123 --> 00:05:47,040
To be specific,

91
00:05:47,123 --> 00:05:49,498
that watered-down
version of Maki named Mai.

92
00:05:49,581 --> 00:05:51,999
Huh?

93
00:05:52,081 --> 00:05:53,666
Oh don't "huh" me.

94
00:05:53,749 --> 00:05:56,624
Even Pepper usually has a
wittier comeback than that one.

95
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:59,666
Why isn't this making her mad?

96
00:05:59,749 --> 00:06:02,582
Instead, I'm the one
getting pissed off!

97
00:06:02,666 --> 00:06:04,458
Oh right, you guys
have your own version

98
00:06:04,542 --> 00:06:05,834
of Pepper don't you?

99
00:06:05,917 --> 00:06:07,001
Yeah, I forgot.

100
00:06:07,083 --> 00:06:09,500
Maybe I should scrap him
and dump the parts somewhere!

101
00:06:09,583 --> 00:06:12,625
(eerie music)

102
00:06:12,709 --> 00:06:13,709
[Panda] Scary.

103
00:06:15,584 --> 00:06:16,668
Huh?

104
00:06:16,751 --> 00:06:19,084
(Panda grunts)

105
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:20,167
Panda, no!

106
00:06:21,626 --> 00:06:25,334
It's a cursed corpse,
so it won't die.

107
00:06:25,418 --> 00:06:27,627
But it won't be able
to move for a while.

108
00:06:28,502 --> 00:06:31,711
Now, who was it you
were going to scrap?

109
00:06:32,627 --> 00:06:34,085
Hold on, Mechamaru.

110
00:06:37,128 --> 00:06:39,295
I'll teach this first-year
she's not quite as cute

111
00:06:39,378 --> 00:06:40,878
as she thinks she is.

112
00:06:40,962 --> 00:06:42,712
I'll show her how
Mai has suffered,

113
00:06:42,795 --> 00:06:44,253
and teach her what it means

114
00:06:44,336 --> 00:06:47,420
for a woman to live
as a jujutsu sorcerer.

115
00:06:47,503 --> 00:06:48,504
Just kidding!

116
00:06:49,504 --> 00:06:51,046
(Panda grunts)

117
00:06:51,129 --> 00:06:53,296
(grunting)

118
00:06:54,129 --> 00:06:55,046
What are you trying to do?

119
00:06:55,129 --> 00:06:57,504
Focus on support and
staying out of sight!

120
00:06:57,587 --> 00:07:00,630
Let's just try to
get along, all right?

121
00:07:00,714 --> 00:07:01,954
Since you and I are so similar.

122
00:07:03,547 --> 00:07:04,964
You idiot puppet!

123
00:07:08,213 --> 00:07:11,881
(mysterious music)

124
00:07:11,965 --> 00:07:13,881
You don't know anything!

125
00:07:15,631 --> 00:07:19,589
Oh good grief, what happened
to us hunting cursed spirits?

126
00:07:19,673 --> 00:07:22,340
Sword option.

127
00:07:22,424 --> 00:07:25,257
(metal clanging)

128
00:07:25,340 --> 00:07:26,382
Boost on.

129
00:07:28,173 --> 00:07:30,382
(blasting)

130
00:07:33,216 --> 00:07:34,133
(gasps)

131
00:07:34,216 --> 00:07:35,216
Ultra Spin!

132
00:07:37,009 --> 00:07:39,009
(blasts)

133
00:07:40,216 --> 00:07:42,592
(tree creaking)

134
00:07:45,592 --> 00:07:48,551
Can't you hold still?

135
00:07:48,634 --> 00:07:49,652
I need to finish this quickly.

136
00:07:49,676 --> 00:07:53,176
I'd rather leave him
be and go help Nobara,

137
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:54,510
but he fires at range.

138
00:07:54,593 --> 00:07:58,593
We didn't have information
on him, Nishimiya, or Miwa.

139
00:07:58,677 --> 00:08:01,176
You're very strong.

140
00:08:01,260 --> 00:08:02,427
What grade are you?

141
00:08:04,845 --> 00:08:07,970
This is my estimate
of everyone's standing.

142
00:08:08,053 --> 00:08:10,428
It's a little more than
Nobara can handle.

143
00:08:10,511 --> 00:08:11,654
I don't think my rating
against cursed spirits

144
00:08:11,678 --> 00:08:14,594
is important right
now, but I'll tell you.

145
00:08:17,220 --> 00:08:18,721
Semi-first-grade.

146
00:08:20,095 --> 00:08:21,013
[Panda] Yikes!

147
00:08:21,095 --> 00:08:22,345
[Mechamaru] Ultra Cannon!

148
00:08:23,679 --> 00:08:25,847
[Panda] His area
of attack is huge!

149
00:08:25,930 --> 00:08:27,805
(blasts)

150
00:08:27,888 --> 00:08:30,179
(dramatic music)

151
00:08:30,263 --> 00:08:32,430
(exhales)

152
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:35,680
Heat emission!

153
00:08:35,763 --> 00:08:38,472
It's a technique with a big
buildup and a long cool-down.

154
00:08:38,556 --> 00:08:40,015
[Mechamaru] This
output is pointless

155
00:08:40,097 --> 00:08:42,015
unless I hit its core dead-on.

156
00:08:43,431 --> 00:08:45,180
[Masamichi Yaga] Cursed corpses.

157
00:08:45,264 --> 00:08:47,557
That's the generic name
for inanimate objects

158
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:50,265
that house curses and
can operate independently.

159
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:54,807
Man-made cursed
corpses always have a core,

160
00:08:54,890 --> 00:08:56,473
which serves as their heart.

161
00:09:00,891 --> 00:09:04,058
I, Yaga Masamichi,
am the leading expert

162
00:09:04,141 --> 00:09:06,474
on puppeteering
cursed techniques,

163
00:09:06,558 --> 00:09:08,850
and Panda is my
ultimate masterpiece.

164
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:11,934
He's a cursed corpse
born with emotions.

165
00:09:15,142 --> 00:09:17,684
(intense music)

166
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:25,019
A cursed corpse mutation.

167
00:09:25,101 --> 00:09:26,101
Panda...

168
00:09:26,143 --> 00:09:28,226
is not a panda!

169
00:09:28,310 --> 00:09:30,518
(thumping)

170
00:09:33,978 --> 00:09:35,061
(shouts)

171
00:09:35,144 --> 00:09:37,436
(grunting)

172
00:09:38,686 --> 00:09:40,853
[Mechamaru] I can't
follow his movements!

173
00:09:40,936 --> 00:09:43,270
(grunting)

174
00:09:43,353 --> 00:09:45,937
(dramatic music)

175
00:09:56,855 --> 00:09:57,771
You know what?

176
00:09:57,855 --> 00:09:59,646
I would have heard rumors

177
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:00,872
if there was someone
out there like me.

178
00:10:00,896 --> 00:10:03,104
So the fact that I haven't

179
00:10:03,187 --> 00:10:04,939
means that you're
not a cursed corpse.

180
00:10:05,023 --> 00:10:06,832
You're a sorcerer who's
remote-controlling this thing

181
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:09,647
while your real
body is elsewhere.

182
00:10:09,731 --> 00:10:13,272
So why get offended at being
treated like a cursed corpse?

183
00:10:13,355 --> 00:10:14,355
Don't wanna be like me?

184
00:10:14,982 --> 00:10:17,148
I feel wounded!

185
00:10:18,356 --> 00:10:20,065
That is so hurtful!

186
00:10:21,398 --> 00:10:22,708
Judging by your high
cursed energy output,

187
00:10:22,732 --> 00:10:26,691
your main body
probably isn't too far away.

188
00:10:26,774 --> 00:10:28,774
It's right outside
the arena, huh?

189
00:10:28,858 --> 00:10:31,316
Guess there's no point
in hunting you down, then.

190
00:10:31,399 --> 00:10:32,834
You'd just be free to
act in the meantime.

191
00:10:32,858 --> 00:10:35,774
So I guess I'll
just bust you up.

192
00:10:35,858 --> 00:10:38,692
You won't be doing
either of those.

193
00:10:38,775 --> 00:10:40,108
Heavenly Pact.

194
00:10:40,191 --> 00:10:41,358
Have you heard of it?

195
00:10:42,358 --> 00:10:43,150
It's not the kind of pact

196
00:10:43,233 --> 00:10:46,150
one would normally
forge with oneself.

197
00:10:46,233 --> 00:10:48,318
This fateful pact
was forced on me

198
00:10:48,401 --> 00:10:50,484
the second I entered this world.

199
00:10:50,568 --> 00:10:52,109
I was born without a right arm

200
00:10:52,192 --> 00:10:54,151
and with nothing at
all below my knees,

201
00:10:54,234 --> 00:10:57,318
and I have no sensation
from the waist down.

202
00:10:57,401 --> 00:11:00,110
My skin is so fragile that
even moonlight burns it.

203
00:11:00,193 --> 00:11:02,485
It feels like needles
are constantly stabbing

204
00:11:02,569 --> 00:11:04,319
into every pore of my body.

205
00:11:04,402 --> 00:11:06,110
But in exchange
I've been granted

206
00:11:06,193 --> 00:11:07,736
immense cursed energy production

207
00:11:07,819 --> 00:11:09,945
and the ability to
use cursed techniques

208
00:11:10,029 --> 00:11:11,029
over vast distances.

209
00:11:11,070 --> 00:11:14,153
I didn't ask for
any of this power.

210
00:11:14,236 --> 00:11:16,528
In fact, if I could trade
my cursed techniques

211
00:11:16,611 --> 00:11:18,737
to have a normal
body, I'd gladly do so.

212
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:22,612
And so, when I see a
cursed corpse like you

213
00:11:22,696 --> 00:11:24,404
walking around in broad daylight

214
00:11:24,487 --> 00:11:25,738
without a care in the world...

215
00:11:25,821 --> 00:11:28,195
instead of me...

216
00:11:28,279 --> 00:11:30,154
I cannot stand it!!

217
00:11:30,237 --> 00:11:32,031
(whirring)

218
00:11:32,113 --> 00:11:33,113
Ultimate Mechamaru!

219
00:11:34,905 --> 00:11:36,947
Mode: Albatross!

220
00:11:39,655 --> 00:11:42,364
[Panda] That's an incredible
amount of cursed energy!

221
00:11:42,448 --> 00:11:44,656
And given his position...

222
00:11:44,740 --> 00:11:46,364
Nobara's in his line of fire!

223
00:11:46,448 --> 00:11:47,448
I have to block it!

224
00:11:47,948 --> 00:11:50,781
[Mechamaru] Ultimate Cannon!

225
00:11:50,865 --> 00:11:53,198
(blasting)

226
00:12:01,657 --> 00:12:03,908
(fire crackling)

227
00:12:03,992 --> 00:12:05,783
Is it dead?

228
00:12:07,325 --> 00:12:11,491
No. The very concept of
death doesn't apply to you.

229
00:12:15,326 --> 00:12:16,844
[Panda] You revealed your
technique while complaining

230
00:12:16,868 --> 00:12:19,035
about your misfortune, earlier.

231
00:12:19,117 --> 00:12:22,035
Quite the sorcerer thing to do.

232
00:12:22,117 --> 00:12:22,951
It's still alive?

233
00:12:23,035 --> 00:12:26,660
After taking a hit
from Ultimate Cannon?

234
00:12:27,118 --> 00:12:28,910
(stomp)

235
00:12:31,327 --> 00:12:33,036
[Panda] I'm kind
of pissed off now.

236
00:12:35,744 --> 00:12:36,160
(Mechamaru's voice quavers)

237
00:12:36,243 --> 00:12:38,453
What form is that?

238
00:12:39,619 --> 00:12:40,494
[Masamichi Yaga] Panda...

239
00:12:40,578 --> 00:12:42,119
is not a panda!

240
00:12:44,328 --> 00:12:47,037
(energetic music)

241
00:12:49,912 --> 00:12:52,287
(energetic music)

242
00:12:55,537 --> 00:12:57,954
(wooden blocks clacking)

243
00:12:58,038 --> 00:12:59,039
Panda...

244
00:13:00,163 --> 00:13:03,246
You should know you
have an older brother

245
00:13:03,330 --> 00:13:04,330
and sister.

246
00:13:06,204 --> 00:13:07,455
No I don't.

247
00:13:07,538 --> 00:13:10,081
Yes, but they're inside of you.

248
00:13:10,164 --> 00:13:12,789
It's hard to explain.

249
00:13:12,873 --> 00:13:13,122
Inside of me?

250
00:13:13,205 --> 00:13:14,122
Yes.

251
00:13:14,205 --> 00:13:17,289
You'll get it someday.

252
00:13:17,372 --> 00:13:20,123
And in the
meantime, those two...

253
00:13:20,206 --> 00:13:23,373
will always be there
to lend you strength.

254
00:13:26,082 --> 00:13:29,373
[Mechamaru] Sword
Option: Ultra Shield!

255
00:13:30,791 --> 00:13:33,166
(metal shattering)

256
00:13:33,249 --> 00:13:35,499
(grunting)

257
00:13:37,166 --> 00:13:38,499
[Panda] Normally a cursed corpse

258
00:13:38,583 --> 00:13:40,333
has a single core for its heart,

259
00:13:40,416 --> 00:13:42,751
but there are three
cores inside me,

260
00:13:42,834 --> 00:13:45,043
and by switching out
which one is the main core,

261
00:13:45,125 --> 00:13:46,584
I can convert my body.

262
00:13:48,084 --> 00:13:51,334
There's the Panda
core, focused on balance,

263
00:13:51,417 --> 00:13:52,960
my older brother, Gorilla Core,

264
00:13:53,044 --> 00:13:55,168
focused on power for
short, decisive battles.

265
00:13:55,251 --> 00:13:58,376
and my bashful older sister.

266
00:13:58,460 --> 00:14:01,002
His first attack got
my older sister's core,

267
00:14:01,085 --> 00:14:03,544
and that last one
exhausted the Panda core!

268
00:14:03,627 --> 00:14:05,919
Now the only choice
I'm left with is...

269
00:14:06,003 --> 00:14:08,586
to beat him with Gorilla Mode!

270
00:14:09,627 --> 00:14:11,336
(boom)

271
00:14:11,419 --> 00:14:14,003
(dramatic music)

272
00:14:16,170 --> 00:14:18,210
[Mechamaru] He doesn't
pack as much power as Toudou.

273
00:14:18,253 --> 00:14:21,004
But that palm strike just now...

274
00:14:21,087 --> 00:14:23,837
went all the way
to my internals.

275
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:27,379
Even if I block it, I'll
still incur damage.

276
00:14:27,463 --> 00:14:29,212
You get it now?

277
00:14:29,296 --> 00:14:31,546
This is Gorilla
Mode's special move!

278
00:14:31,629 --> 00:14:32,254
(beats chest)

279
00:14:32,338 --> 00:14:34,921
The unstoppable Drumming Beat!

280
00:14:36,505 --> 00:14:38,065
[Mechamaru] If I take
that Drumming Beat

281
00:14:38,130 --> 00:14:39,881
to my head or chest,

282
00:14:39,964 --> 00:14:41,604
I won't be able to move
Mechamaru anymore.

283
00:14:43,339 --> 00:14:45,419
My right arm's Sword Option
is no longer functioning.

284
00:14:47,298 --> 00:14:49,214
I can't fire Ultimate
Cannon anymore, either.

285
00:14:49,298 --> 00:14:52,049
[Panda] Gorilla Mode
pounds through cursed energy

286
00:14:52,131 --> 00:14:54,757
like a gorilla, but
I need to hurry.

287
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:55,757
I crushed his right arm,

288
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:58,632
so he can't fire off his
ultimate attack anymore.

289
00:14:58,716 --> 00:15:01,257
And with no swords
in his left or his mouth,

290
00:15:01,341 --> 00:15:03,215
he only has ranged blasts left.

291
00:15:03,299 --> 00:15:06,424
Even so, he won't
fire them randomly.

292
00:15:06,507 --> 00:15:08,150
Mechamaru believes he's
already failed to finish me

293
00:15:08,174 --> 00:15:11,759
with those blasts
twice, when the truth is,

294
00:15:11,842 --> 00:15:14,884
he actually put two of
my cores close to death.

295
00:15:14,967 --> 00:15:18,092
His next move is to blast my
core with point-blank precision

296
00:15:18,175 --> 00:15:20,801
or try to finish
me with a slash.

297
00:15:20,885 --> 00:15:21,885
However...

298
00:15:24,718 --> 00:15:27,468
(energetic music)

299
00:15:29,176 --> 00:15:32,177
at close range, I
have the advantage!

300
00:15:32,260 --> 00:15:35,510
(energetic rock music)

301
00:15:39,094 --> 00:15:42,054
(grunting)

302
00:15:56,554 --> 00:15:59,137
(intense music)

303
00:16:30,265 --> 00:16:33,307
(grunting)

304
00:16:52,267 --> 00:16:53,184
A tile?

305
00:16:53,267 --> 00:16:55,392
Did he pick it off
the roof just now?

306
00:16:56,809 --> 00:16:58,935
(grunts)

307
00:17:02,602 --> 00:17:05,185
First a distraction,
then jet acceleration!

308
00:17:05,268 --> 00:17:07,393
He's experienced at this!

309
00:17:07,477 --> 00:17:09,603
[Mechamaru] This
time, I won't miss!

310
00:17:09,686 --> 00:17:13,227
His cursed energy
is densest at his core!

311
00:17:13,311 --> 00:17:14,686
Right here!

312
00:17:17,853 --> 00:17:19,937
(groans)

313
00:17:22,854 --> 00:17:25,854
You did well for a mere puppet.

314
00:17:28,312 --> 00:17:29,604
(grunts)

315
00:17:29,687 --> 00:17:30,688
(gasps)

316
00:17:30,772 --> 00:17:32,664
[Panda] Don't treat me
like other cursed corpses.

317
00:17:32,688 --> 00:17:34,772
I know how to bluff
the position of my core

318
00:17:34,855 --> 00:17:37,229
with cursed energy manipulation.

319
00:17:37,313 --> 00:17:39,605
I've already concealed
the number of cores I have.

320
00:17:42,856 --> 00:17:44,856
(grunts)

321
00:17:50,147 --> 00:17:51,814
(tiles shattering)

322
00:17:51,898 --> 00:17:54,440
You lost because you
underestimated puppets.

323
00:17:54,523 --> 00:17:56,315
I haven't had a single
thing in common

324
00:17:56,398 --> 00:17:58,318
with anyone around me
from the moment I was born.

325
00:18:00,690 --> 00:18:03,191
I thought maybe you and
I could relate to each other

326
00:18:03,274 --> 00:18:04,274
because of that.

327
00:18:06,191 --> 00:18:09,983
But I'm not jealous of
humans, and I never have been.

328
00:18:10,067 --> 00:18:10,649
You're not?

329
00:18:10,733 --> 00:18:13,358
I mean, humans are creepy.

330
00:18:13,441 --> 00:18:14,442
(gasps)

331
00:18:15,734 --> 00:18:16,817
(soft piano music)

332
00:18:16,901 --> 00:18:18,484
They'll risk their
lives and fight hard

333
00:18:18,567 --> 00:18:20,817
to reach their goals,
then suddenly turn around

334
00:18:20,901 --> 00:18:22,817
and be laid-back or wishy-washy.

335
00:18:22,901 --> 00:18:24,068
I don't get them.

336
00:18:25,360 --> 00:18:27,818
Still, I do love those
aspects that I don't have,

337
00:18:27,902 --> 00:18:28,902
creepy as they are.

338
00:18:30,318 --> 00:18:33,276
You have your own
hardships too, Mechamaru.

339
00:18:33,360 --> 00:18:36,903
But just having more hardships
doesn't make you right.

340
00:18:37,402 --> 00:18:40,861
It's not like we're
enemies in the first place.

341
00:18:40,944 --> 00:18:43,028
I mean, why'd you
become a sorcerer?

342
00:18:43,111 --> 00:18:46,152
Was it just the only thing
you thought you could do?

343
00:18:46,235 --> 00:18:47,737
Not that it makes
any difference.

344
00:18:48,320 --> 00:18:51,487
But if you want to do
something else with your life...

345
00:18:51,570 --> 00:18:53,236
I'd help you.

346
00:18:55,987 --> 00:18:57,696
(sighs)

347
00:18:57,780 --> 00:19:00,237
Mechamaru, don't waste
your powerful moves.

348
00:19:00,321 --> 00:19:04,113
The foe in front of you
may not be the only one.

349
00:19:06,113 --> 00:19:08,655
Mechamaru, someone
who can't instantly state

350
00:19:08,739 --> 00:19:10,322
his type of woman can never be

351
00:19:10,405 --> 00:19:12,655
a full-fledged jujutsu sorcerer.

352
00:19:13,614 --> 00:19:17,322
Mechamaru, instead of
chocolate I got you some of these!

353
00:19:17,405 --> 00:19:20,406
I heard the double A Evoltas
are one of your favorites.

354
00:19:20,490 --> 00:19:22,156
[Mechamaru] I'm
not built like that.

355
00:19:22,239 --> 00:19:23,490
(gasps)

356
00:19:23,573 --> 00:19:26,865
-Liars!
-(laughing)

357
00:19:26,948 --> 00:19:27,948
One day...

358
00:19:30,074 --> 00:19:31,324
(sloshing)

359
00:19:38,199 --> 00:19:40,991
(soft piano music)

360
00:19:45,283 --> 00:19:47,700
I'll be together with everyone.

361
00:19:50,283 --> 00:19:51,593
[Panda] Hm? Did
you say something?

362
00:19:51,617 --> 00:19:54,743
I wonder if you'll
still say you'll help me

363
00:19:54,826 --> 00:19:56,451
after you see what I look like.

364
00:19:56,534 --> 00:19:57,409
Huh?

365
00:19:57,493 --> 00:19:58,409
(laughing)

366
00:19:58,493 --> 00:20:00,743
You think someone
who looks like me

367
00:20:00,826 --> 00:20:02,910
is gonna fuss over
what you look like?

368
00:20:02,994 --> 00:20:03,994
I'm a panda!

369
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:08,078
Later.

370
00:20:08,160 --> 00:20:10,036
Let me pay you
a visit next time.

371
00:20:15,079 --> 00:20:16,620
Shut up damn puppet.

372
00:20:22,995 --> 00:20:23,453
Oh, I forgot...

373
00:20:23,536 --> 00:20:24,536
Huh?

374
00:20:28,121 --> 00:20:29,954
[Panda] Lend me your phone.

375
00:20:30,038 --> 00:20:32,329
(birds whistling)

376
00:20:32,412 --> 00:20:34,621
(swords clanging)

377
00:20:34,704 --> 00:20:36,955
(grunting)

378
00:20:39,830 --> 00:20:40,330
[Miwa Kasumi] No way!

379
00:20:40,413 --> 00:20:42,955
This woman...

380
00:20:43,039 --> 00:20:44,622
is incredibly strong!

381
00:20:46,330 --> 00:20:49,247
(closing theme music)

382
00:20:56,123 --> 00:20:59,874
(singing in Japanese)

383
00:22:15,589 --> 00:22:17,672
-(quirky music)
-[Mechamaru] Juju Stroll.

384
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:22,464
Mechamaru, I need
you to let Noritoshi know

385
00:22:22,547 --> 00:22:24,673
Utahime's calling him.

386
00:22:26,007 --> 00:22:26,840
Mechamaru?

387
00:22:26,924 --> 00:22:30,132
Please, take this
book to Toudou, okay?

388
00:22:31,465 --> 00:22:32,382
Mechamaru!

389
00:22:32,465 --> 00:22:33,757
Perfect timing.

390
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:36,133
Please, could you deliver
this box to Toudou and Kamo?

391
00:22:39,341 --> 00:22:40,549
What the hell?

392
00:22:40,633 --> 00:22:42,508
What do I look like,
your messenger boy?

393
00:22:42,591 --> 00:22:43,591
(gasps)

394
00:22:43,674 --> 00:22:45,925
(curious music)

395
00:22:46,008 --> 00:22:47,926
Don't try to talk
to me right now.

396
00:22:49,342 --> 00:22:51,467
Takada's live-streaming
and I intend to watch it!

397
00:22:53,842 --> 00:22:55,384
Ibaragi?

398
00:22:55,467 --> 00:22:56,967
You mean Ibaraki.

399
00:22:57,051 --> 00:22:59,426
So how is it that
you don't know that?

400
00:23:00,760 --> 00:23:02,927
[Both] Uh, because they're
too much trouble, obviously.

401
00:23:07,843 --> 00:23:12,928
[Miwa] To be honest, I'm
still scared of both of them.

402
00:23:13,011 --> 00:23:14,594
[All] But if I admit that,

403
00:23:14,677 --> 00:23:17,594
I might not be able to
ask him favors anymore.

404
00:23:19,678 --> 00:23:21,970
-Mechamaru?
-Hm?

405
00:23:22,054 --> 00:23:22,637
(exciting music)

406
00:23:22,720 --> 00:23:24,970
We're all counting on you!

407
00:23:25,054 --> 00:23:26,678
Yeah!

408
00:23:26,762 --> 00:23:27,678
(gasps)

409
00:23:27,762 --> 00:23:29,762
[All] Gotta run! Time
for our missions!

410
00:23:29,845 --> 00:23:31,763
Wait!

411
00:23:31,846 --> 00:23:32,846
Why?

412
00:23:34,846 --> 00:23:37,638
(gentle guitar music)

413
00:23:37,721 --> 00:23:38,721
Oh well.

414
00:23:39,721 --> 00:23:41,555
It's good that they
can rely on me...

415
00:23:43,263 --> 00:23:44,263
I guess.

416
00:23:44,639 --> 00:23:47,014
(intense music)

417
00:23:47,098 --> 00:23:50,847
(singing in Japanese)

